---
/**
 * The stat band: the size of the library in one line, under the catalog wall.
 *
 * Founder, 2026-11-07: "hundreds of videos, hundreds of sources combined into
 * one place... can we build perceived value in the first three seconds?"
 *
 * Seven of the eight figures are DERIVED at build time from the lesson files
 * and the measured narration timings, so none of them can drift from what is
 * actually published. The exception is the word count, which is the existing
 * "1.5M+" claim carried over from CURRICULUM_STATS and is the one number here
 * a human wrote. It is deliberately approximate and marked below.
 *
 * Numbers are rendered in full for screen readers. "1.5M+" is an abbreviation
 * a screen reader would spell out letter by letter, so it is aria-hidden with
 * a spoken sentence beside it, the same pattern StatBanner.astro uses.
 */
import { CURRICULUM_METRICS } from '../../data/curriculum-metrics';

interface Stat {
	value: string;
	label: string;
	/** Spoken sentence used when `value` is an abbreviation. */
	srText?: string;
}

const m = CURRICULUM_METRICS;

/** The headline figure, given its own cell and the audio mark. */
const lead: Stat = {
	value: m.narrationHours.toFixed(1),
	label: 'hours of narrated audio',
};

const stats: Stat[] = [
	{ value: String(m.liveLessons), label: 'lessons' },
	{ value: String(m.manifestTracks), label: 'tracks' },
	{ value: String(m.narratedLessons), label: 'lessons with word-level read-along' },
	{ value: String(m.citedSources), label: 'cited sources' },
	{ value: String(m.arxivPapers), label: 'arXiv papers' },
	// The one figure not derived. See the note at the top of this file.
	{ value: '1.5M+', label: 'words', srText: 'More than 1.5 million words' },
];
---

<section class="v2-stats" aria-label="Clawdemy at a glance">
	<ul class="v2-stats__grid" role="list">
		<li class="v2-stat v2-stat--lead">
			<span class="v2-stat__icon" aria-hidden="true">
				<svg
					viewBox="0 0 24 24"
					width="26"
					height="26"
					fill="none"
					stroke="currentColor"
					stroke-width="1.8"
					stroke-linecap="round"
					stroke-linejoin="round"
				>
					<path d="M3 18v-6a9 9 0 0 1 18 0v6"></path>
					<path
						d="M21 19a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-1a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-3a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h3zM3 19a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h1a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-3a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H3z"
					></path>
				</svg>
			</span>
			<span class="v2-stat__num">{lead.value}</span>
			<span class="v2-stat__label">{lead.label}</span>
		</li>
		{
			stats.map((stat) => (
				<li class="v2-stat">
					{stat.srText ? (
						<>
							<span class="sr-only">{stat.srText}</span>
							<span class="v2-stat__num" aria-hidden="true">
								{stat.value}
							</span>
							<span class="v2-stat__label" aria-hidden="true">
								{stat.label}
							</span>
						</>
					) : (
						<>
							<span class="v2-stat__num">{stat.value}</span>
							<span class="v2-stat__label">{stat.label}</span>
						</>
					)}
				</li>
			))
		}
		<li class="v2-stat v2-stat--free">
			<span class="v2-stat__num">Free</span>
			<span class="v2-stat__label">no signup, no paywall, no ads</span>
		</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<style>
	/* GSD's mock, reproduced here because the mock stylesheet is an audit
	   artifact and not part of this build. Every colour is an existing token.
	   --v2-wrap carries a fallback so this component is correct on its own,
	   before the shared page wrap lands with the rest of the sections. */
	.v2-stats__grid {
		list-style: none;
		margin-block: 0;
		margin-inline: auto;
		max-width: var(--v2-wrap, 90rem);
		padding-inline: var(--fl-gutter);
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1.7fr repeat(7, minmax(0, 1fr));
	}

	.v2-stat {
		padding: 1.15rem 0.9rem;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.2rem;
		justify-content: center;
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.v2-stat + .v2-stat {
		border-left: 1px solid var(--fl-line);
	}

	.v2-stat__num {
		font-family: var(--fl-display);
		/* A figure is one token: "1.5M+" breaking after the M reads as two
		   numbers. The clamp floor keeps it narrow enough not to overflow. */
		white-space: nowrap;
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.3vw, 2.05rem);
		font-weight: 800;
		line-height: 1.05;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: var(--fl-ink);
	}

	.v2-stat__label {
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		line-height: 1.3;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}

	.v2-stat--lead {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
		grid-template-rows: auto auto;
		column-gap: 0.85rem;
		align-content: center;
		padding-left: 0;
		padding-right: 1.2rem;
	}

	.v2-stat--lead .v2-stat__icon {
		grid-row: span 2;
		align-self: center;
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		width: 3.25rem;
		height: 3.25rem;
		border-radius: 14px;
		color: var(--clawdemy-blue);
		background: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
	}

	.v2-stat--lead .v2-stat__num {
		font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 3.6vw, 3rem);
		color: var(--clawdemy-blue);
	}

	.v2-stat--lead .v2-stat__label {
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		color: var(--fl-ink);
	}

	.v2-stat--free .v2-stat__num {
		color: var(--lp-teal);
	}

	/* Eight cells in a row stop fitting well before the page does. */
	@media (max-width: 75rem) {
		.v2-stats__grid {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
		}

		.v2-stat--lead {
			grid-column: span 4;
			padding-left: 0;
			border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fl-line);
		}

		.v2-stat:nth-child(2),
		.v2-stat:nth-child(6) {
			border-left: 0;
		}

		.v2-stat:nth-child(n + 6) {
			border-top: 1px solid var(--fl-line);
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 40rem) {
		.v2-stats__grid {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		}

		.v2-stat--lead {
			grid-column: span 2;
			border-top: 0;
		}

		.v2-stat {
			padding: 0.9rem 0.75rem;
		}

		.v2-stat:nth-child(n) {
			border-left: 0;
			border-top: 1px solid var(--fl-line);
		}

		.v2-stat:nth-child(odd):not(.v2-stat--lead) {
			border-left: 1px solid var(--fl-line);
		}

		.v2-stat:nth-child(2),
		.v2-stat:nth-child(3) {
			border-top: 0;
		}
	}
</style>
